    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="1dd96ff8-f7cd-5a2f-bbea-a3619676d66e" activityNameId="f94ab722-f8db-5441-8933-b84620c6ba36" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, ventilation system, Geschäftshaus C, Esslingen, various components</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, ventilation system, Geschäftshaus C, Esslingen, various components
Disposal of various components for a ventilation system for an office building with offices only (no kitchen, restaurant or car park). The inventory is based on a building with a total heated gross floor area of 2621 m2 and a total nominal air flow of 4000 m3/h, total weight of the components: 1210 kg/Unit, building with a specific air flow rate of 1.5 m3/h per m2 heated gross floor area. Data from call of bid including components for air valves, air intake, roof-hoods, dampers, fire dampers, silencers and sensors.;
UUID: d8d4decd-e811-4f31-89fa-5ccec8abb9dc
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location: Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland.
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Metal pieces, copper in cables and electronic devices are recycled, plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes (e.g. rock wool) are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2013. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: na
Sampling: Waste-specific calculation based on production input data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_d8d4decd-e811-4f31-89fa-5ccec8abb9dc.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
